:"","html_url":"https://github.com/apaszke","id":4583066,"login":"apaszke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODMwNjY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4583066?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apaszke","id":4583066,"login":"apaszke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODMwNjY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apaszke","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"### Description\r\n\r\nI have a **custom-call** bwd operation that takes `x (4, 4, 8)`, `invvar (4, 1)`, `weight (4, 8)`, and `grad_output (4, 4, 8)`.  It produces `grad_input (4, 4, 8)`, `grad_weight (4, 8)`, and `scratch (16, 32)`.\r\n\r\nI am running this bwd operation with `x`, `invvar`, `grad_output`, and `grad_input` sharded on the batch dimension (leftmost dim), and `weight`, `grad_weight`, and `scratch` replicated, using `xmap` manual sharding:\r\n\r\n```python\r\njax.config.update(\"experimental_xmap_spmd_lowering\", True)\r\njax.config.update(\"experimental_xmap_spmd_lowering_manual\", True)\r\nweight = jax.numpy.ones((4, 8), dtype=numpy.float32)\r\ng = jax.random.normal(prng_key, (4, 4, 8))\r\n\r\nout, res = jax_ext.fwd(x, weight)\r\n\r\njitted_out = jax.jit(\r\n    partial(jax_ext._bwd_p.bind, eps=1e-05)\r\n)(g, *res)\r\nwith Mesh(numpy.array(jax.devices()).reshape(4), (\"a\")):\r\n\r\n    def xmap_bwd(res, g):\r\n        invvar, x, weight = res\r\n        invvar_sharded = invvar.reshape(4, 1)\r\n        x_sharded = x.reshape(4, 4, 8)\r\n        g_sharded = g.reshape(4, 4, 8)\r\n        axes = (\"a\", None, None)\r\n        xmapped = xmap(\r\n            partial(\r\n                jax_ext._bwd_p.bind, eps=1e-05\r\n            ),\r\n            in_axes=(axes, (\"a\", None), axes, (None, None)),\r\n            out_axes=[axes, (None, None), (None, None)],\r\n            axis_resources={\"a\": \"a\"},\r\n        )\r\n        xmapped_out = xmapped(g_sharded, invvar_sharded, x_sharded, weight)\r\n        return xmapped_out\r\n\r\n    pjitted = pjit(\r\n        xmap_bwd,\r\n        in_axis_resources=(\r\n            (\r\n                PartitionSpec(\r\n                    None,\r\n                ),\r\n                PartitionSpec(None, None, None),\r\n                PartitionSpec(None, None),\r\n            ),\r\n            PartitionSpec(None, None, None),\r\n        ),\r\n        out_axis_resources=[\r\n            PartitionSpec(None, None, None),\r\n            PartitionSpec(None, None),\r\n            PartitionSpec(None, None),\r\n        ],\r\n    )\r\n    print(jax.make_jaxpr(pjitted)(res, g))\r\n    pjitted.lower(res, g).compiler_ir().dump()\r\n    pjitted_out = pjitted(res, g)\r\n\r\nprint(f\"jitted_out: {jitted_out}\")\r\nprint(f\"pjitted_out: {pjitted_out}\")\r\nprint(numpy.allclose(jitted_out[0], pjitted_out[0]))\r\nprint(numpy.allclose(jitted_out[1], pjitted_out[1]))\r\nprint(numpy.allclose(jitted_out[2], pjitted_out[2]))\r\n```\r\n\r\nAs `grad_weight` is a replicated array, each device gets its own buffer but they populate the buffers with different values, making it an **\"unreduced\"** array.  For my use case, the values in all buffers need to be summed to produce the correct final values for `grad_weight`.\r\n\r\nWhat can I do to produce **\"reduced\"** `grad_input`?\r\n\r\n### What jax/jaxlib version are you using?\r\n\r\njax/jaxlib 0.3.16 built on 08/11/2022 with TF cfc45e1027d43cf54b0358d7d9e2fc01f58938dd\r\n\r\n### Which accelerator(s) are you using?\r\n\r\nGPU\r\n\r\n### Additional System Info\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_at":"2022-08-23T20:22:54Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/883319?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/seanprime7","id":883319,"login":"seanprime7","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MzMxOQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanprime7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments":2,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11941/comments","created_at":"2022-08-16T17:42:03Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11941/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11941","id":1340679150,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"tot